\begin{Verbatim}[frame=single,fontsize=\footnotesize,formatcom=\color{bl}]
         Baseline  Response Selected  Family.q Retained.q Seconds
Fixed    2.414646 0.2112196 2.625866 0.2939532  0.2939532   0.061
Variable 2.439239 0.2046192 2.643859 0.2939532  0.3161700   0.565
\end{Verbatim}

Allowing variable retention increases the predicted selected mean by
approximately 0.017993 under the same total resources. The baseline rises
by approximately 0.024593 while the response falls by approximately
0.006600. The family-slot metric stays unchanged, whereas the nominal
retained metric reflects the unequal retained weights.

An independent numerical reference enumerated 455 family sets and
83,950 admissible two-budget assignments per set, or 38,197,250 candidates.
It matches this selected plan and objective. This additional validation
does not change the optimizer's printed \cde{best.found} status or its
own bound gap. Agreement concerns the numerical objective under the supplied normal
model and fitted marker effects.

The seconds column contains one elapsed-time observation for each optimizer
call. It excludes the common data preparation and subsequent evaluation.
The variable-retention implementation uses the equivalent small-count
normal integrals and shared cache described in the appendix; its work
ceiling and requested objective remain explicit.

\section{Selection-aware contributions and selected DH genotypes}
\label{sec:selected-genotypes}

Unequal retained counts change the nominal parental shares shown above.
Selection within each family can also change which parent's chromosome
segments occur in its retained descendants. The optional
\cde{genetic.model} combines the fitted additive effects, effect-allele
coding, marker map and a declared within-family ranking law. It supports
an analytic contribution prediction and an explicit assessment of actual
DH origin paths under that same fixed genetic model.

The example uses the same six candidate founders, fifteen allowed pairs
and production and retention budgets as
Section~\ref{sec:retained-allocation}. The marker data set
\cde{cross.parents} supplies the 243 complete model markers and all thirty
rows for the fixed genomic-reference frequencies. Only the six eligible
founders become candidate parents. Uniform weights describe origin
averaged over all 243 markers, including the 109 markers with identical
alleles across those six founders. They do not identify unobserved physical
genome lengths.

The declared population is an immediate DH generation from the F1, with
a cM Haldane map and no additional intermating. The index model combines
standardized genetic value with independent normal noise at the requested
accuracy. Here accuracy one ranks the fitted genetic values directly,
with neutral random resolution of ties. The original supplied kinship
matrix retains its scale and reference.

The first calculation reports selected contributions without adding a
contribution cap. Its count-search problem and settings match the preceding
calculation. The requested genotype scenarios run once after the final
plan is accepted; they do not run for every candidate allocation.

<<eval=FALSE>>=
genetic.time <- system.time({
    genetic.plan <- st.cross.plan(
        merit = cross.merit[practical.ids],    # The same six candidate founders
        K = practical.K,                       # The original named kinship reference
        n.crosses = 3,                         # Three produced biological families
        theta = max(diag(practical.K)),        # The original family-slot ceiling
        upper = 0.5,                           # The original family-slot parent bound
        scores = practical.scores,             # The same precise cross means and variances
        criterion = "usefulness",              # Expected selected G1 mean
        accuracy = 1,                          # Ranking by the fitted genetic value
        progeny = list(                        # The same production and retention budgets
            total.progeny = 90,                # Produced DH descendants
            total.selected = 12,               # Retained DH descendants
            min.progeny = 4,                   # Minimum produced from each active pair
            max.progeny = 50,                  # Maximum produced from each active pair
            min.selected = 1,                  # At least one retained from each family
            max.selected = 12,                 # Retention also remains below production
            selection.method =                 # Finite-normal selection prediction
                "order.statistics",
            control = list(                    # Cumulative count-search settings
                algorithm = "auto",            # Supported bounded integer search
                max.transitions = 1e7          # Shared count-work ceiling
            )
        ),
        genetic.model = list(                  # Optional additive genotype model
            data.set = "cross.parents",        # Thirty-row fixed genomic reference
            population = "DH",                 # Immediate F1-derived DH descendants
            t = 0,                             # No additional intermating generation
            map.function = "Haldane",          # cM map with independent crossovers
            index.model =                      # Declared independent-noise index law
                "trait.independent.noise",
            marker.weights = NULL,             # Uniform weights on all model markers
            selected.founder.theta = NULL,     # Contributions reported without a new cap
            scenarios = list(                  # Final genotype assessment only
                replicates = 250,              # Independent retained-population replicates
                seed = 12052026                # Reproducible private scenario bank
            ),
            control = list(                    # Whole-call genetic resource settings
                max.cells = 1e7,               # Genetic workspace and snapshot budget
                max.work = 1e8                 # Cumulative genetic-work ceiling
            )
        ),
        control = list(                        # The same reproducible family search
            method = "heuristic",              # Bounded best-found family search
            start = joint.plan,                # The same actual starting counts
            seed = 1,                          # The same local optimizer seed
            starts = 1,                        # One checked starting plan
            maxit = 2000                       # The same outer iteration ceiling
        )
    )
})
genetic.plan
@

\begin{Verbatim}[frame=single,fontsize=\footnotesize,formatcom=\color{bl}]
Joint production and retention planning
Criterion: usefulness; status: best.found
Produced families: 3.0000; produced descendants: 90.0000; retained
  descendants: 12.0000
Families with retained descendants: 3.0000; selection: order.statistics
