% INTERPRETATION: future-plan
The printed objective concerns the complete training bank and horizon two.
Its unselected G1 baseline, actual G1 response and additional G2 response
have the component identity given in the appendix. Existing G1 gain and
usefulness fields retain their analytic meaning. The returned search
status and unknown expectation gap remain part of the result.

In the printed family order, produced counts are $(34,50,6)$ and retained
counts are $(3,8,1)$. All 32 training replicates and 256 evaluation
replicates complete. The search reaches its training-work allowance and
retains \cde{best.found} status. Completion of the evaluation bank does
not close the optimization gap.

The separate evaluation bank compares the chosen design with the actual
equal-count and G1-focused designs. Its whole common replicates generate
both generations for every qualified comparator. This assessment does
not reuse the earlier single-cycle scenario numbers or rank training
proposals by held-out performance.

