% INTERPRETATION: future-differences
Every difference is the future-focused plan minus the named comparator.
The SE comes from the corresponding difference inside each common
replicate, rather than combining unrelated aggregate SEs. The additional
G2 response is the selected G2 mean minus the selected G1 mean for that
same design. Interpretation of an advantage follows the actual paired
estimate and its precision; a training winner need not improve the
held-out expectation estimate.

Relative to the G1-focused design, current selected mean falls by
approximately 0.000359 and the additional G2 response falls by 0.000034.
The net G2 difference is $-0.000393$ with MCSE 0.000576, approximately
0.68 MCSE below the G1-focused comparator. The held-out assessment
therefore provides no demonstrated advantage over the G1-focused design.
The difference from equal counts is $+0.005698$ with MCSE 0.002029,
approximately 2.8 MCSE above zero under this fitted model and declared
simulation policy.

The training score is approximately 2.7992, while the held-out mean is
2.79263. This illustrates the risk of overfitting a small fixed training
bank. The search optimizes its sampled objective; its selected design
and numerical status do not certify the optimum of the unknown
expectation. The seeds, requested bank sizes and constraints remain
those declared before this comparison.

