The variance is conditional on each actual selected-DH pair and describes
the DH progeny of its new F1. Mean conditional variance and mean
conditional SD summarize different aspects of that next-cycle
segregation. The square root of mean variance does not replace mean SD
or the actual G2 calculation.

For the selected design, mean conditional variance is approximately
0.009226 and mean conditional SD is 0.093665. The square root of the
first number is approximately 0.09605, showing the distinction in this
actual example.

